From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: abox: bound CPU votes before access and reject failed CALL votes

The CPU gear request-table search can finish one element beyond the array.
The old code reads that element for call/PM bookkeeping and writes its value
and ID before checking the bounds. Reject table exhaustion before any such
access or side effect, retaining the existing ENOMEM diagnostic and result.
An existing ID remains updateable even when all table slots are occupied.

Return enqueue failure immediately from the synchronous wrapper. CALL PCM
open must propagate its per-endpoint CPU vote failure before requesting L2
or sending PCM_OPEN: no vote was installed, so no rollback is needed on this
branch. Existing L2-failure cleanup retains its endpoint-specific vote key.
The normal successful path and ordinary per-DAI votes are unchanged.

This handles a concrete out-of-bounds/error-propagation defect. It does not
serialize concurrent request-table insertion, propagate asynchronous clock
programming failures, or establish a fix for the captured ABOX MMU fault.
Based on the pinned Samsung driver; applies after patches 0017 and 0018.

diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -3307,19 +3307,19 @@
 			request++) {
 	}
 
-	abox_check_call_cpu_gear(dev, data, request->id, request->value,
-			id, gear);
-
-	request->value = gear;
-	wmb(); /* value is read only when id is valid */
-	request->id = id;
-
 	if (request - data->ca7_gear_requests >= len) {
 		dev_err(dev, "%s: out of index. id=%x, gear=%u\n", __func__,
 				id, gear);
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 
+	abox_check_call_cpu_gear(dev, data, request->id, request->value,
+			id, gear);
+
+	request->value = gear;
+	wmb(); /* value is read only when id is valid */
+	request->id = id;
+
 	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &data->change_cpu_gear_work);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -3330,6 +3330,8 @@
 {
 	int result = abox_request_cpu_gear(dev, data, id, gear);
 
+	if (result < 0)
+		return result;
 	flush_work(&data->change_cpu_gear_work);
 	return result;
 }

